From 80c3434b68e3107366d9c4d90d8dd4079603b43e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:53:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] sepolicy: keep vold's fstrim out of /persist, quietly

vold's daily fstrim walks every fstab mount point and was denied
reading /persist. That partition (calibration, the secure-world key
store) is 64 MB and rarely written: no need to trim it or to let vold
in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/vold.te | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/vold.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/vold.te b/sepolicy/vold.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1748336
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/vold.te
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+# vold's daily fstrim walks every fstab mount point; /persist (calibration, the secure-world key
+# store) is 64 MB and rarely written, so trimming it gains nothing: keep vold out, quietly.
+dontaudit vold persist_file:dir read;
-- 
2.53.0

